{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.minus_six_admissible_not_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.minus_six_admissible_not_unique","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L332-L338","doc":"`−6` is admissible under both hypothesis sets and unique under neither.  This\nis the file's bottom line in one statement: the route narrows, and does not\nselect. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.hurwitz_admissible_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.hurwitz_admissible_chi","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L325-L330","doc":"The admissible Euler characteristics under the **self-contained** §3 bound\nalone (`2 ≤ g ≤ 8`), with no classification input.  Seven values, a genuine\nnarrowing from the infinite set that Steps 3–4 leave, and not to `−6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.classification_admissible_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.classification_admissible_chi","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L319-L323","doc":"The admissible Euler characteristics after the **classification** (genus 2,\nplus Laing & Singerman's `g ∈ {3, 4}` as completed by Reyes-Carocca &\nSpeziali Theorem 2).  `−6` is in the list, and so are two others. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.hyperelliptic_simple_iff_genus_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.hyperelliptic_simple_iff_genus_two","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L303-L317","doc":"Genus 2 is the *only* genus at which the hyperelliptic datum is simple: the\ndoubled weight equals 2 exactly there.  So §4's witnesses start at `g = 3`,\nand `g = 2` is a genuine member of the admissible set rather than another\nAccola–Maclachlan counterexample. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.genus_two_transitive_and_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.genus_two_transitive_and_simple","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L293-L301","doc":"**Genus 2 satisfies both hypotheses.**  The hyperelliptic point count, the\ntotal weight and the doubled weight all agree at `g = 2`: six simple\nWeierstrass points.  (At `g = 2` the hyperelliptic datum *is* the general\ndatum — every genus-2 surface is hyperelliptic.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.accola_points_ne_totalWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.accola_points_ne_totalWeight","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L264-L275","doc":"Consequently the datum's point-count misses `totalWeight` at every genus\n`≥ 3` — i.e. `|W| < g³ − g`, the inequality that makes it invisible to a\ntheorem hypothesising `g³ − g` Weierstrass points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.accola_datum_not_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.accola_datum_not_simple","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L253-L262","doc":"**The datum fails simplicity at every genus `≥ 3`**: the common weight is\n`g(g−1)/2 ≥ 3`, never `1`.  So the Accola–Maclachlan curves are transitive\n(H1) and non-simple (¬H2) at every genus from 3 up — they are exactly the\nwitnesses that transitivity alone classifies nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.accola_datum_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.accola_datum_total","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L240-L251","doc":"**The datum is consistent at every genus `≥ 2`.**  `|W| · (2w) = 2 · (g³ − g)`,\ni.e. the `2g + 2` hyperelliptic Weierstrass points of weight `g(g−1)/2` carry\nexactly the total Weierstrass weight.  Stated at `g = k + 2` so that `g ≥ 2`\nis structural rather than a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.twiceHyperellipticWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.twiceHyperellipticWeight","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L235-L238","doc":"**Twice** the Weierstrass weight of a hyperelliptic Weierstrass point at\ngenus `g`.  The weight is `g(g−1)/2`, the maximum possible; doubling keeps\nthe file free of `ℕ`-division. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.hyperellipticPoints","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.hyperellipticPoints","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L232-L233","doc":"Weierstrass-point count of a hyperelliptic surface of genus `g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.eight_is_sharp_for_this_argument","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.eight_is_sharp_for_this_argument","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L209-L214","doc":"The bound of `genus_le_eight` is **attained by the arithmetic**, i.e. the\nproof is not throwing away a factor: at `g = 8` the inequality\n`g(g + 1) ≤ 84` still holds, and at `g = 9` it fails.  So `8` is the exact\ncut-off of this argument, not an artefact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.genus_le_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.genus_le_eight","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L178-L207","doc":"**Transitivity + simplicity + Hurwitz ⟹ `g ≤ 8`.**\n\n`hsimple` is (H2) (`|W| = g³ − g`); `horbit` is (H1) via orbit–stabiliser\n(a single orbit has size dividing, hence at most, the group order);\n`hhurwitz` is Hurwitz's `|Aut(X)| ≤ 84(g − 1)`, valid for `g ≥ 2`.\n\nDerived here rather than cited: it is strictly weaker than Laing &\nSingerman's `g ∈ {3, 4}`, and unlike that theorem it depends on no source\nthis corpus does not hold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.totalWeight_eq_cube_sub_table","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.totalWeight_eq_cube_sub_table","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L158-L163","doc":"The exposed-factor form really is `g³ − g`, checked across `g = 2 … 12`, the\nrange §3 and §5 care about.  A wrong `totalWeight` fails this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L154-L156","doc":"Euler characteristic of a closed orientable genus-`g` surface (matching\n`BranchPointSixNotForced.eulerChar`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.totalWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.totalWeight","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L150-L152","doc":"Total Weierstrass weight of a genus-`g` surface, `g³ − g`, written so the\n`(g − 1)` factor is exposed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.weight_constant_of_transitive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.weight_constant_of_transitive","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/WeierstrassTransitivityNotForced.lean#L124-L137","doc":"**(H1) ⟹ equal weights.**  If a group acts transitively on `P` and `w : P → ℕ`\nis invariant under the action, then `w` is constant.\n\nRead on a compact Riemann surface of genus `≥ 2`: `P` is the Weierstrass\nlocus, `w` the Weierstrass weight, the action that of `Aut(X)`.  Invariance is\nautomatic (the weight is defined from the gap sequence, which an automorphism\ncarries along), so transitivity alone gives constancy. ","signatureChunk":0}]}